evels of public involvement."}, {"id": "B", "text": "It compares citizen science with laboratory experiments in detail."}, {"id": "C", "text": "It argues that amateur researchers produce unreliable data."}, {"id": "D", "text": "It traces the history of citizen science from the 19th century."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Citizen science", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citizen_science', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M19-TS006', 'A', ARRAY['A']::TEXT[], 'The text moves from definition and scope, to fields, to the roles volunteers play in research.', '{"C": "The text presents citizen science as improving research capacity, not as unreliable.", "D": "No historical timeline is given.", "B": "Designed experiments are mentioned once as something observations can complement, with no detailed comparison."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
